1. Introduction & Problem Statement
Digital content delivery networks (CDNs) currently suffer from critical technical and human adoption structural vulnerabilities:
Mandatory Identity Harvesting: Government regulations force platforms to collect biometric, passport, or credit card data to gate standard content.
Financial Intermediary Control: Centralized payment rails reserve the right to freeze accounts, withhold creator revenues, or enforce 30-to-60-day payout holds.
Over-Engineered Crypto Protocols: Early Web3 video attempts failed by placing heavy video transcoding and state-chain settlement on layer-1 or layer-2 smart contracts, leading to cost surges, buffering, and massive onboarding friction.
Token Velocity & Liquidity Freeze Vulnerabilities: Unstructured team allocations, destructive token burn mechanisms, and un-capped "Watch-to-Earn" bot farming drain network liquidity and make content prohibitively expensive as token prices appreciate.
Mobile Engine, Sybil & Concurrency Vulnerabilities: Web3 media apps frequently break on mobile browsers due to Safari audio context revokes and thread-freezing, while federated networks suffer from minute 03:00 paywall DDoS surges, rogue node ad-farming sybil attacks, WebRTC chunk poisoning, and lingering CDN edge cache retention of deleted media.
Human Infrastructure & Real-World Friction Gaps: Theoretical Web3 protocols fail in the real world due to creator migration inertia ("Cold-Start"), node operator legal liability risks, banking chargeback fraud, and tool fatigue from juggling fragmented Web2 platforms.
ProofTube v2.14 resolves these issues by anchoring video streaming to open primitives—decoupling Identity via Nostr, Video Delivery via PeerTube WebRTC mesh with client checksum verification, Monetization via a Universal Multi-Chain Router with threshold top-ups, Network Sustainability via an 8-decimal recycled token model with 4-year founder vesting, and real-world adoption via an All-in-One 7-platform bridge hub, a Locked Escrow Vault, an OpenTimestamp-anchored Primary Authenticity Engine, node compliance shields, self-custody wallet exports, and a unified creator suite.
