3.2 The Primary Authenticity Engine (Bitcoin Block-Anchored Honesty)
To ensure creators maintain honest publishing habits without relying on human judges or unverified client-side timestamps, the protocol enforces Primary Status using immutable, code-based cryptographic verification:
OpenTimestamps / Bitcoin Block Anchoring (The 24-Hour Lead Rule): To prevent creators from spoofing Nostr event timestamps (created_at), a video payload's publication time on ProofTube is verified against an OpenTimestamps Bitcoin block hash proof or verified relay arrival receipt hash. Node background daemons verify that this block-anchored timestamp is at least 24 hours prior to the Web2 release timestamp on YouTube, Rumble, Substack, Telegram, Kick, Odysee, or Fountain (or maintains 90% catalog parity over a rolling 30-day window).
Automated Grace Period & Re-Lock: If a creator violates the lead rule on consecutive uploads, the smart contract automatically pauses direct withdrawals and routes their 45% ad earnings back into the Locked Escrow Vault. Once the creator restores their 24-hour lead publishing habit for 14 consecutive days, the vault unlocks automatically.
