B.2 Execution Mechanics
Segmented Video Encryption at Encoding (ffmpeg): The transcoding queue encrypts post-minute-3 HLS segments (.ts) with a unique 16-byte AES-128 key, leaving segments 00:00 to 03:00 unencrypted:
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -hls_time 4 -hls_key_info_file key_info.txt -hls_playlist_type vod stream.m3u8


Minute 01:00 Pre-Fetched L402 Challenge: At playback minute 01:00, the client player automatically issues a background request for the locked key at /api/v1/keys/{video_id}_locked. The L402 proxy returns an HTTP 402 payment challenge.
Background Settlement & Zero-Buffering Playback: The persistent Service Worker thread settles the invoice via WebLN, NWC, or Session Top-Up between minute 01:00 and minute 03:00. Upon receiving the HTTP 200 OK containing the 16-byte AES-128 key, the key is held in RAM. When video playback reaches minute 03:00, the stream decrypts instantly without playback stutter or node proxy server surges.
